From 5e46f22b567f900f6841fbf8807d63eb0e17d598 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Heimpold <mhei@heimpold.de>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:51:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] c++: include signal.h outside the gensios namespace

The C++ wrapper includes gensio.h inside namespace gensios. On POSIX
systems, gensio_os_funcs.h also includes signal.h, which can pull in
additional system headers. If those headers are first included within
the namespace, their declarations are not available in the global scope.
Header guards then prevent subsequent includes from providing the global
declarations expected by other system headers.

On AArch64 Linux, including sys/prctl.h after gensio/gensio can therefore
fail because __u64 and __u32 were declared inside namespace gensios.

Include signal.h before entering the namespace so its declarations and
those of its transitive system headers remain in the global scope.

Signed-off-by: Michael Heimpold <mhei@heimpold.de>
---
 c++/include/gensio/gensioosh | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/c++/include/gensio/gensioosh b/c++/include/gensio/gensioosh
index 64d593fffc3b..c1e9215da80c 100644
--- a/c++/include/gensio/gensioosh
+++ b/c++/include/gensio/gensioosh
@@ -9,6 +9,10 @@
 #ifndef GENSIOOSH_CPP_INCLUDE
 #define GENSIOOSH_CPP_INCLUDE
 
+#ifndef _WIN32
+#include <signal.h>
+#endif
+
 #include <string>
 #include <stdexcept>
 #include <atomic>
